WEBVTT

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:15.680
Ten years have passed since the Council of the Hundred and One last gathered.

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:19.990
Councilors, what is the meaning of this?

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:22.370
Refrain from acting oblivious.

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:25.000
This is about your country's invasion of JIOR.

00:00:25.330 --> 00:00:29.880
I believe that the Council's policy is to not get involved in the affairs of mankind.

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:34.180
A certain weapon has been brought to our attention. I believe it's called the "Valvrave".

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:37.890
Our reports identify it as a level three phenomenon.

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:41.380
You opposed the Magius?!

00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:43.270
We know all about it.

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:48.520
You trespassed the domain of the Magius and kept it secret from us.

00:00:48.830 --> 00:00:54.690
It pains me to admit that I did not notice its relation to the Magius.

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:57.410
We were simply acting in response to a military threat and—

00:00:57.410 --> 00:00:59.410
Colonel Cain Dressel.

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:04.100
He served as your right hand man in the revolution

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:07.000
and led your forces in the conflict.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:07.920
No, not him...

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:12.100
He has been a Magius for ten years now.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:12.840
Furthermore,

00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:15.090
you will become one as well.

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:29.900
Abandon thy body, and embrace a new one.

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:34.030
Abandon thy body, and embrace a new one.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:35.480
What in God's name?

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:58.320
Try harder.

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:35.150
What?

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:40.280
Unit 6?!

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:41.450
Who's piloting it?

00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:44.300
Don't worry, Shoko. I'll finish this up quickly.

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:48.740
Another new unit?!

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:50.500
Who cares?!

00:03:51.170 --> 00:03:51.750
Hey!

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:11.560
Oh, what a cute little hack!

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:24.020
The Colonel hijacked it?

00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:26.030
A-Drei! We've gotta get out!

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:28.080
What happened to using the escape pods of the Ideal?

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:30.410
Can't use those! The engine's blown!

00:04:52.730 --> 00:04:55.230
Damn JIOR!

00:05:03.610 --> 00:05:04.780
Haruto!

00:05:19.470 --> 00:05:21.420
Pino... Pino...

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:24.170
Brother! Brother!

00:05:24.570 --> 00:05:28.180
I thought so. So this is the original pair.

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:30.810
It won't work! I lost control!

00:05:31.170 --> 00:05:33.060
What's up with this engine?

00:05:41.630 --> 00:05:42.820
Brother?

00:05:44.390 --> 00:05:45.990
Brother!

00:05:50.690 --> 00:05:52.790
It's overloading!

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:53.240
Prue!

00:05:55.550 --> 00:05:58.460
It's not very gentlemanly to damage a vessel on its maiden flight.

00:05:59.470 --> 00:06:01.130
Kriemhild, do you read me?

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:04.380
Prepare to withdraw!

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:07.130
Retreat while assisting the Colonel!

00:06:13.810 --> 00:06:16.100
This gear's slow as molasses!

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:18.900
Retreat! Q-Vier, I know you can hear me!

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:20.740
Just let me finish it off first!

00:06:20.740 --> 00:06:21.560
Retreat!

00:06:48.890 --> 00:06:52.550
What? What <i>are</i> the Valvraves?

00:06:53.310 --> 00:06:56.060
We barely escaped defeat.

00:07:02.670 --> 00:07:05.160
Year 71 of the True Calendar.

00:07:05.160 --> 00:07:13.400
Two months have passed since Module 77 arrived at the neutral territory of the Moon, escaping the Dorssian attack.

00:07:14.150 --> 00:07:18.080
They called the Dorssian invasion of JIOR illegitimate,

00:07:18.550 --> 00:07:23.460
and claimed to be the rightful successors of JIOR in international politics.

00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:27.960
The world celebrated them as tragic heroes.

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:32.220
Tokishima Haruto became the symbol of the struggle against Dorssia.

00:07:32.870 --> 00:07:37.120
Rukino Saki's song was sang around the world in support of the students,

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:40.480
and became an international bestseller.

00:07:40.950 --> 00:07:48.480
They received supplies and financial support, and seemed to have achieved peace.

00:07:49.290 --> 00:07:50.490
However...

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:53.490
We, the ARUS, simply cannot accept this.

00:07:53.830 --> 00:07:55.720
Huh? Why's that?

00:07:55.720 --> 00:07:59.680
We would only let the JIORians who are stranded abroad into the Module!

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:03.250
It presents a risk of Dorssian spies infiltrating the country.

00:08:03.250 --> 00:08:07.880
For that reason, we will keep handling border control ourselves.

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:10.510
At least allow doctors and politicians through!

00:08:10.510 --> 00:08:15.140
We will provide you with the necessary personnel.

00:08:15.530 --> 00:08:17.900
Next, regarding the foreign supplies.

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:19.900
We're concerned that you won't be able to handle it all on your own.

00:08:19.900 --> 00:08:21.160
Well...

00:08:21.160 --> 00:08:23.640
Do you have anyone who is qualified to be an accountant?

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:25.400
Even having held a simple accounting job would be enough.

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:26.270
Uh...

00:08:26.670 --> 00:08:29.420
Let's move on the next topic, then.

00:08:29.420 --> 00:08:31.190
Please look at page 314.

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:36.700
This is about overseeing the health hazards of imported goods.

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:39.080
We will handle this for you as well.

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:40.330
You don't mind, right?

00:08:44.690 --> 00:08:47.620
The gaps between the fits are getting shorter.

00:08:47.620 --> 00:08:50.960
Then it really is related to the time spent in the Valvrave.

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:54.930
I can only conclude that the runes are real.

00:08:54.930 --> 00:08:58.760
That would explain a number of phenomena.

00:08:58.760 --> 00:09:00.600
What about the OS girl in Unit 1?

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:04.020
Silent. Did it really talk?

00:09:05.250 --> 00:09:06.650
What are you doing?!

00:09:06.650 --> 00:09:08.650
Haruto, are you okay?

00:09:11.970 --> 00:09:13.650
Haruto! Haruto!

00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:20.600
You liar! You said it was just a routine checkup! He's not a guinea pig!

00:09:20.600 --> 00:09:22.410
It's okay...

00:09:23.690 --> 00:09:25.410
I asked for this...

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:29.670
Tokishima Haruto himself suggested this experiment.

00:09:30.530 --> 00:09:34.520
We need to find out more about the Valvraves and the holy spirits.

00:09:34.520 --> 00:09:37.300
There's no need to lock him up for that!

00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:41.430
He requested it to prevent him from attacking people.

00:09:45.070 --> 00:09:49.380
I can't let that happen ever again...

00:09:50.030 --> 00:09:50.940
So...

00:09:51.860 --> 00:09:53.120
Haruto...

00:10:26.050 --> 00:10:30.500
With time, they will lose the support and approval of the people.

00:10:31.010 --> 00:10:32.600
It doesn't matter how powerful their weapons are.

00:10:32.600 --> 00:10:34.980
If they are locked in a battle of attrition, they will have to surrender.

00:10:36.370 --> 00:10:39.240
Let me guess. Straight from our beloved Colonel Cain's mouth.

00:10:39.870 --> 00:10:42.300
You've been quite spiteful lately.

00:10:42.300 --> 00:10:45.870
Did something happen when you retrieved the Valvrave?

00:10:57.470 --> 00:10:59.400
You know, X,

00:11:01.010 --> 00:11:04.920
we're the only ones left in our year.

00:11:05.750 --> 00:11:06.930
That's right.

00:11:07.730 --> 00:11:08.930
So...

00:11:11.730 --> 00:11:15.440
We are only here because of Colonel Cain.

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:38.710
We <i>are</i> going to Earth, but we're not going to war.

00:11:38.710 --> 00:11:41.840
L-Elf called it reconnaissance.

00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:42.940
But still...

00:11:42.940 --> 00:11:47.430
If you see my family, please tell them that I'm fine.

00:11:47.430 --> 00:11:49.820
You look gorgeous, Takahi!

00:11:49.820 --> 00:11:52.320
Of course. You're the ones who made this uniform.

00:11:52.320 --> 00:11:53.720
It'd be a shame not to show it off.

00:11:53.720 --> 00:11:56.140
Thanks! You can't wear your school uniform forever.

00:11:56.140 --> 00:11:58.440
Please come back safely!

00:12:01.450 --> 00:12:05.320
Introduction to international law

00:12:01.450 --> 00:12:05.320
International politics

00:12:01.450 --> 00:12:05.320
International law precedents

00:12:09.430 --> 00:12:12.900
Prime minister, it's time for the seeing off ceremony.

00:12:13.430 --> 00:12:17.630
People are so nice, but countries are a whole different story.

00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:18.780
They're merciless.

00:12:18.780 --> 00:12:21.300
That is why we are going to Earth.

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:23.100
We want to find out if any countries mean us harm

00:12:23.100 --> 00:12:26.660
and we're also to display our willingness to use military force.

00:12:26.660 --> 00:12:28.620
You need something to pressure with for negotiations.

00:12:28.620 --> 00:12:29.720
The operation will—

00:12:30.570 --> 00:12:31.920
Is that your dinner?

00:12:31.920 --> 00:12:32.980
Nice and light, isn't it?

00:12:33.290 --> 00:12:35.100
Add some supplements.

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:37.240
Taste is one thing, but—

00:12:37.240 --> 00:12:38.360
You're worried for me?

00:12:38.990 --> 00:12:41.620
Caring for your health is part of my job.

00:12:41.620 --> 00:12:46.120
You will have to take charge of Module 77 once we depart for Earth.

00:12:46.490 --> 00:12:48.700
Yeah, leave it to me.

00:12:48.700 --> 00:12:51.620
I'll hold the fort until all of you come back.

00:12:52.350 --> 00:12:55.020
That's my fight.

00:12:56.150 --> 00:12:59.130
Ah, naming rights?

00:12:59.130 --> 00:13:00.760
What the hell?

00:13:00.760 --> 00:13:04.680
I'm getting paid to call it Beast High.

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:07.680
You really like that shit, don't you?

00:13:07.680 --> 00:13:09.140
What are you talking about?

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:12.480
Awaken the beast within you!

00:13:12.480 --> 00:13:13.320
Huh?

00:13:13.320 --> 00:13:16.270
Beast High! You know. The commercial?

00:13:17.770 --> 00:13:20.080
Energy drink Beast High!

00:13:20.080 --> 00:13:21.720
Now on sale!

00:13:21.720 --> 00:13:24.160
Awaken the beast within!

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:28.940
Never heard of it.

00:13:28.940 --> 00:13:31.950
Huh? But it's so popular.

00:13:36.110 --> 00:13:37.210
Haruto!

00:13:37.930 --> 00:13:40.960
Is it time to go?

00:13:40.960 --> 00:13:43.920
Do you really want to go like that?

00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:48.380
I'll be fine. I'll be in the cockpit the entire time.

00:13:49.530 --> 00:13:50.580
Haruto!

00:13:52.490 --> 00:13:54.140
This is so weird...

00:13:54.140 --> 00:13:56.390
Must be because I locked myself in.

00:14:02.790 --> 00:14:05.820
See? I'm fine.

00:14:11.030 --> 00:14:13.490
I don't know why,

00:14:13.490 --> 00:14:14.580
but I know it worked.

00:14:16.580 --> 00:14:21.960
It went away after we did it, didn't it?

00:14:23.550 --> 00:14:28.700
If I ever had a fit like that, I'd rather it was with you.

00:14:39.730 --> 00:14:40.850
No.

00:14:41.650 --> 00:14:42.780
Haruto!

00:14:45.550 --> 00:14:49.020
I'll be counting on you. Everyone's worried about their families.

00:14:49.020 --> 00:14:50.800
Did you tell Haruto, too?

00:14:50.800 --> 00:14:52.940
This isn't the time.

00:14:53.730 --> 00:14:55.580
I can worry about myself later.

00:14:56.650 --> 00:14:59.830
That's how a prime minister should act.

00:15:07.650 --> 00:15:09.170
Rukino Saki?

00:15:11.230 --> 00:15:13.180
Is Haruto with you?

00:15:13.180 --> 00:15:15.930
No. Did something happen to Tokishima Haruto?

00:15:15.930 --> 00:15:17.520
I lost him!

00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:19.810
Though I doubt he'd go very far in his situation.

00:15:20.150 --> 00:15:21.900
Did something happen to Haruto?

00:15:24.060 --> 00:15:25.320
The colors...

00:15:32.790 --> 00:15:34.240
What's going on, doc?!

00:15:34.630 --> 00:15:35.740
What?

00:15:39.670 --> 00:15:42.000
It won't move. But why?

00:15:42.830 --> 00:15:44.790
The runes dried out?

00:15:45.500 --> 00:15:51.680
Central exit

00:15:52.430 --> 00:15:56.740
The harbor... If I can get to the cockpit...

00:15:56.740 --> 00:15:57.940
Tokishima Haruto.

00:15:59.510 --> 00:16:00.950
How did you find me?

00:16:00.950 --> 00:16:05.300
I placed a tracking device on you the other day.

00:16:05.930 --> 00:16:07.400
That's so like you.

00:16:08.110 --> 00:16:10.080
Take me to Unit 1.

00:16:10.590 --> 00:16:12.450
I can barely stand.

00:16:12.930 --> 00:16:15.640
The Valvraves have stopped functioning.

00:16:15.640 --> 00:16:16.700
The problem is with you.

00:16:17.090 --> 00:16:18.610
What?!

00:16:18.610 --> 00:16:19.980
They're out of energy.

00:16:20.590 --> 00:16:24.580
Now that you mention it, we never refueled them.

00:16:25.070 --> 00:16:28.880
Despite their size, the Valvraves pack more power than a warship.

00:16:28.880 --> 00:16:32.090
However, they don't use conventional fuel.

00:16:32.550 --> 00:16:35.470
They are powered by runes.

00:16:36.030 --> 00:16:37.320
Runes?

00:16:37.320 --> 00:16:41.180
Information particles that mankind is yet to discover.

00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:42.600
That's what they are.

00:16:43.030 --> 00:16:47.860
Just how material consists of particles, information consists of runes.

00:16:48.510 --> 00:16:54.740
I guess that applies to our DNA, language, and emotions as well.

00:16:54.740 --> 00:16:57.740
Therefore the richest source of runes...

00:16:58.590 --> 00:16:59.660
...are humans.

00:17:01.950 --> 00:17:03.160
No way...

00:17:03.810 --> 00:17:06.180
So when I attack people...

00:17:06.180 --> 00:17:09.560
You're actually collecting runes for the Valvraves.

00:17:09.560 --> 00:17:17.340
Will I have to?

00:17:17.690 --> 00:17:19.920
The contract has been made.

00:17:19.920 --> 00:17:22.180
You belong to the Valvraves now.

00:17:22.180 --> 00:17:24.480
You exist at the cost of the lives of others.

00:17:24.480 --> 00:17:26.370
That's insane!

00:17:26.370 --> 00:17:27.730
I'm done with this crap!

00:17:28.790 --> 00:17:29.730
I see.

00:17:34.610 --> 00:17:36.040
Then die.

00:17:37.370 --> 00:17:41.620
You may be invinvible, but I'm quite sure that beheading you should do the trick.

00:17:41.620 --> 00:17:45.370
Die? Me?

00:17:45.830 --> 00:17:51.880
Then I wouldn't cause any more trouble. I wouldn't hurt anyone.

00:17:54.790 --> 00:17:59.140
If only I... If only the holy spirit was gone...

00:18:03.290 --> 00:18:05.740
If I...

00:18:07.170 --> 00:18:08.020
No.

00:18:08.630 --> 00:18:09.540
No!

00:18:12.410 --> 00:18:16.400
L-Elf, what will happen to the Valvraves if I die?

00:18:16.750 --> 00:18:18.960
A new pilot will be chosen.

00:18:18.960 --> 00:18:22.030
This country needs the military power of the Valvraves.

00:18:24.110 --> 00:18:25.520
I take back what I said.

00:18:27.290 --> 00:18:31.290
The curse of the Valvraves is mine to bear.

00:18:31.290 --> 00:18:35.170
We can't go to Earth without the Valvraves!

00:18:35.170 --> 00:18:39.560
The Dorssian forces are waiting just outside the neutral zone!

00:18:39.560 --> 00:18:42.180
We can't even leave the Moon, let alone go to Earth!

00:18:42.690 --> 00:18:46.680
Can you do it? Can you attack people to save people?

00:18:47.290 --> 00:18:48.690
I'll do it.

00:18:48.690 --> 00:18:51.940
The fits are rune withdrawal symptoms.

00:18:52.350 --> 00:18:55.940
If you're regularly provided with rune, you won't attack people.

00:18:56.650 --> 00:19:01.200
L-Elf. I'm gonna feed only on you from now on.

00:19:02.050 --> 00:19:03.950
I won't hurt anyone else.

00:19:04.650 --> 00:19:05.920
We'll split it fifty-fifty.

00:19:06.450 --> 00:19:08.460
Curse, hope, the whole deal.

00:19:53.010 --> 00:19:53.860
It's on.

00:20:02.380 --> 00:20:04.720
Another day of nothing to report.

00:20:04.720 --> 00:20:06.180
They sure know how to stay put.

00:20:06.180 --> 00:20:08.060
It's safe to stay on the Moon.

00:20:08.060 --> 00:20:10.420
Who'd be stupid enough to leave that haven?

00:20:11.670 --> 00:20:15.400
Detecting something exiting Module 77 at high speed!

00:20:18.850 --> 00:20:21.820
Five Valvraves and a Ripple class ship!

00:20:21.820 --> 00:20:24.560
You will leave the neutral zone in 60 seconds.

00:20:24.560 --> 00:20:26.320
A battlefield awaits you there.

00:20:29.890 --> 00:20:31.160
We're crossing the line!

00:20:31.530 --> 00:20:32.780
That's the Dorssian army!

00:20:32.780 --> 00:20:35.540
Units 3, 4, and 6, follow Unit 1 in formation.

00:20:35.950 --> 00:20:37.920
Unit 5, protect this ship.

00:20:40.430 --> 00:20:42.000
We're going to Earth.

00:20:42.550 --> 00:20:46.050
We're going to Earth to find JIORians,

00:20:46.750 --> 00:20:48.580
and the people who made the Valvraves.

00:20:49.410 --> 00:20:53.690
And I'll ask them how to return to being human!

00:20:54.690 --> 00:20:56.190
We're past the line!

00:21:36.990 --> 00:21:39.000
After retaking JIOR and all that was lost,

00:21:39.000 --> 00:21:40.760
once it's all over,

00:21:41.750 --> 00:21:45.320
I'll destroy the Valvraves.

00:21:45.990 --> 00:21:49.820
This curse will end with me.

00:23:39.930 --> 00:23:42.270
It's been a while, Mirko.

00:23:42.990 --> 00:23:46.020
This isn't the Council of the Hundred and One.

00:23:47.050 --> 00:23:53.540
Here, I am Amadeus, the 68th Führer of Dorssia.

00:23:54.710 --> 00:23:57.300
I'll keep that in mind when around humans.

00:23:58.550 --> 00:23:59.540
More importantly, though...

00:24:00.390 --> 00:24:01.290
Look at that.

00:24:02.070 --> 00:24:06.300
Yes, the children of the Valvrave.

00:24:12.470 --> 00:24:14.890
PREVIEW

00:24:13.890 --> 00:24:16.350
Next time: episode fourteen.

00:24:16.730 --> 00:24:18.560
Siblings in the atmosphere.

00:24:19.390 --> 00:24:24.980
Valvrave the Liberator... The system that unveils the world.

00:24:24.980 --> 00:24:27.480
EPISODE 14

00:24:24.980 --> 00:24:27.480
Siblings in the atmosphere
